From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 14:03:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?phlink:=20phase=205-06a=20=E2=80=94=20adblock?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20prefs=20+=20global=20runtime=20gate?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the user-facing master switch and per-site exception list for the
phlink adblocker, mirrored into a process-global runtime gate consumed
by both the URLLoaderThrottle and the cosmetic-filter Mojo host.

Changes
-------
* New profile prefs (default-on, syncable):
  - phlink.adblock.enabled        (bool,   default true)
  - phlink.adblock.exceptions     (list,   default [])

* New EngineProvider runtime gate:
  - SetEnabled / IsEnabled        (atomic bool, lock-free read)
  - SetExceptionDomains            (lock-protected unordered_set)
  - IsActiveForUrl(GURL)          — returns false when disabled, when
    the URL is non-http(s), or when the URL's registrable domain
    (eTLD+1) is in the exception set. Raw-IP / localhost (no
    registrable domain) is treated as active.

* New per-profile KeyedService AdblockSettingsService:
  - Observes both prefs via PrefChangeRegistrar and pushes them to
    EngineProvider on every change. Created with the browser context.
  - ProfileSelection::kOwnInstance for regular; kNone for guest.
    Incognito inherits its parent's prefs.

* PhlinkAdblockThrottle:
  - WillStartRequest gates on IsActiveForUrl(source_url) so the user's
    "disable on this site" exception correctly suppresses subresource
    blocking for that page.
  - WillRedirectRequest gates on IsEnabled (master switch only) since
    RedirectInfo doesn't always carry a usable source URL; the next
    internally-restarted load passes through WillStartRequest.

* CosmeticFilterHost::GetCosmeticResources gates on IsActiveForUrl;
  inactive frames receive empty hide_selectors / injected_script.

* Wiring:
  - chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc registers the new prefs.
  - chrome/browser/profiles/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc
    constructs AdblockSettingsServiceFactory at startup.
  - chrome/browser/prefs:impl and
    chrome/browser/profiles:profiles_extra_parts_impl pick up the new
    deps on //chrome/browser/phlink/adblock:phlink_adblock.

* Unit tests (10 → 13 passing):
  - PhlinkAdblockEngineProviderGateTest.MasterSwitchOff
  - PhlinkAdblockEngineProviderGateTest.NonHttpSchemeInactive
  - PhlinkAdblockEngineProviderGateTest.ExceptionDomainSuppressesActivity

Refs phlink PRD §6.1 (adblock UX), plan 5-06.

The chrome://settings/phlink/adblock UI lands in 5-06b once Phase 8
brings the settings UI infra. Until then the prefs are settable via
the Preferences JSON.
